{
  "requirement": "For a Cargo workspace that depends on `habeas`, interactive `cargo agents sync` MUST let the user enable Habeas's plugin. Once enabled, it MUST make the skills shipped with the selected Habeas version available to configured agents. After the selected version changes, `cargo agents sync` MUST provide the skills shipped with the new version.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the requirement is met. The implementation is complete and the test covers all three obligations.\n\n**Implementation**\n\nThe obligations are carried out by declarative Symposium plugin metadata in `Cargo.toml`. Each part is marked `{impl}`:\n- `[package.metadata.symposium] name = \"habeas\"` (line 24–25) defines the plugin carried by the `habeas` crate. Symposium discovers it for any workspace that depends on `habeas`.\n- `[package.metadata.symposium.defaults] skills = false` (line 28–29) keeps the skills off by default. The user therefore has to choose to enable the plugin, which is the \"let the user enable\" obligation.\n- `[[package.metadata.symposium.skills]] source.path = \"assets/skills\"` (line 32–33) publishes the skills directory that ships inside the selected crate version. Skills therefore come from the selected Habeas version, and a version change brings in that version's skills.\n\nThe `[package]` table has no `include` or `exclude`, so `assets/skills` is packaged with the crate. The other symposium entries (`installations`, `hooks`) are marked for the separate requirements `symposium_cli` and `symposium_setup_hook`. They are not unspecified behavior of this subject.\n\n**Tests**\n\n`tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py` is marked `{test}` for this requirement and runs in the CI `symposium-hook` job. It uses a real `cargo-agents` binary against a temporary consumer project that depends on `habeas`:\n- **Enabling:** `interactive_sync` drives `cargo agents sync` through a pty. It waits for the \"Enable it?\" prompt and moves off the default \"ask later\" choice. It then asserts that the decision was recorded (`auto-enable` and `habeas` in the saved config) and that the hook registration exists.\n- **Skills available:** it asserts that every skill under `assets/skills` is installed byte-identically into `.agents/skills/` for the configured codex agent.\n- **Version change:** it points the consumer at a \"next\" crate whose version is one patch higher and whose first skill is modified. It confirms through `cargo metadata` that Cargo selects the new version. It then runs `cargo agents sync` and asserts that the installed skill now matches the new content. It allows for Symposium's debounce and caching.\n\n**Minor limits**\n\nThese do not amount to a gap:\n- The test uses a single-package project rather than a multi-member workspace.\n- It does not exercise declining the prompt.\n- The behavior is fully delegated to Symposium's plugin mechanism, and the smoke test exercises that mechanism end to end.",
  "references": "88b07b1ed831317cb8e9f7ab1af1ebbaaddc2b67b99320ef3e91d6295719d5dd",
